  "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4-x,\\,a=0,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (4-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
